From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: the controllers as DirectInput joysticks too (Wine patch
 0927)

In xinput mode a game that reads its controller with DirectInput, or
with winmm's joystick calls, found none: they look through the HID
stack, which a title can't run. Wine patch 0927 makes each player's
controller a DirectInput joystick as Windows shows an Xbox 360
controller, so those games find it, and a game that reads Xbox
controllers with XInput still leaves it out of DirectInput.
---
