+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
+Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] dinput: The PS5 title's controllers as DirectInput joysticks.
+
+DirectInput finds joysticks through the HID stack, which a PS5 title
+can't run, so in xinput mode a game that reads its controller with
+DirectInput (or winmm's joystick calls, which go through DirectInput)
+found none: only XInput and Windows.Gaming.Input saw the title's
+controllers (patches 0470, 0477 and 0926).
+
+Each title controller that is connected is now a joystick as Windows
+shows an Xbox 360 controller: "Controller (XBOX 360 For Windows)",
+045e:028e, a gamepad; X and Y the left stick, Rx and Ry the right one,
+Z both triggers (the left one up from the middle, the right one down),
+the D-pad a hat and ten buttons, in Windows' order. As on Windows it has
+no force feedback, and its path names it an XInput device (IG_00 to
+IG_03), so a game that reads such controllers with XInput leaves it out
+here. While acquired, a waitable timer has the input thread read it
+every 4 ms, so buffered data and event notification work as for a HID
+joystick; GetDeviceState and Poll read it at once. A controller that
+disconnects makes its device unplugged. Anywhere but in a title the
+Unix library finds no title and nothing changes.
